 "kind": "skeleton",
 "title": "Find in a list",
 "caption": "The page is one container. Its header holds the title, a line under it and the main action. Its content is two parts: the filter bar, and the records, which reach the outline with no room around them. Its footer holds the paging. The records are one data table on every screen: in its TABLE layout at a desktop and a tablet, and in its LIST layout on a phone, where each record is a line in the style of an item: its picture, its name, and under the name its state and one more fact. The filter bar is drawn as the filter bar widget draws it: the filter icon, which is a mark and so a circle; the boxes that share its width equally; the action that shows the filters that are hidden; and, after a line that sets them apart, the two actions that search and clear. On a tablet it holds fewer boxes. On a phone it is one button that says how many filters are on, with the action that clears them. The lines of the LIST layout have a line between each two. A state that is normal shows no badge. A press on a row opens the record, and the actions of a row are behind one action at its end. A tablet shows fewer columns than a desktop.",
